  "notes": [
    "A run counts only if it finished and its verify command exited 0. Cells need at least 3 counted runs; any failed or errored run in a cell voids it.",
    "Worker tokens are quota on the opencode-go and Gemini subscriptions, including cache reads. They are never converted to USD and are not part of the Claude cost.",
    "Small tasks cost more with the swarm: where the work is only a few lines, delegation adds overhead. Value scales with writing volume, not file count.",
    "Wall time includes waiting for headless workers and varies a lot between runs; the range columns show the full spread, not a typical value.",
    "Claude cost, model, turns and duration come from the run transcript (last result event, cumulative); bench/compare.py recorded only the first result event of a session.",
    "Turns are summed over the result segments of a session. 'stock' runs in older files are reported as 'vanilla'.",
    "Different models never share a cell. The 'vs vanilla' ratio is shown only against a published vanilla cell of the same case and model; otherwise it is n/a.",
    "Voided cells are never shown with numbers, even when later runs in the same cell passed.",
    "Case scaffold: cells use different models (claude-opus-5-5, claude-sonnet-5-5), so cost ratios against vanilla are only given within the same model."
